# Experiment Log

## Purpose

Record completed or materially changed experiments for <strong>{{PROJECT_NAME}}</strong>. Keep implementation, delivery, and general validation work in `03_active_work\WORK_PROGRESS.en.md`.

## Active method identity

- <strong>Method, model, process, or experimental contract:</strong> Unconfirmed during initialization.
- <strong>Lifecycle:</strong> `unconfirmed`.
- <strong>Evidence authority:</strong> `reference-only` until the method and validity boundary are confirmed.

## {{DATE}} — Experiment log initialized

- <strong>Question or hypothesis:</strong> Unconfirmed.
- <strong>Inputs and identity:</strong> Unconfirmed.
- <strong>Method and execution:</strong> No project-specific experiment was run by initialization.
- <strong>Results and failures:</strong> None recorded.
- <strong>Evidence limits:</strong> The presence of this file does not establish a completed experiment.
- <strong>Retained artifacts:</strong> None confirmed.
- <strong>Decision and handoff:</strong> Inspect project evidence before adding an experiment entry.

## Entry format

Add new entries newest first. Record the question, exact inputs and method identity, execution and deviations, results and failures, evidence limits, retained artifacts, decision outcome, and handoff.

## Maintenance

Append every completed or materially changed experiment. When the active method identity changes, move superseded detailed entries into a recoverable archive package, state their lifecycle and evidence authority, and leave a concise restoration pointer here.
